Planned assessment
| Objective | Evidence or example shown | Learner task | What earns credit |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| O1 — Describe what a rolling restart does | A three-instance web app restarted one instance at a time while it serves traffic. Show a simulated status line: A serving, B restarting, C serving. | What happens to an app's instances during a rolling restart? | States that instances are replaced in batches. |
| O2 — Explain when a rolling restart keeps capacity | A three-instance web app restarted one instance at a time while it serves traffic. Show a simulated status line: A serving, B restarting, C serving. | Why does a single-instance app lose capacity during a rolling restart? | Explains the more-than-one-instance condition. |
| O3 — Handle the objection that rolling restarts guarantee zero downtime | A three-instance web app restarted one instance at a time while it serves traffic. Show a simulated status line: A serving, B restarting, C serving. | A customer says rolling restarts guarantee zero downtime. What do you say? | Corrects the claim without dismissing the customer and agrees a next step. |

